# Paths and task names `mise run docs-links` must not treat as broken.
#
# Format: <entry> [# reason]. Three legitimate categories only:
#
#   - Planned-but-unwritten docs a design doc or live plan forward-references.
#     Remove the entry when the doc lands.
#   - Paths that belong to an upstream repo (freedesktop-sdk, gnome-build-meta,
#     dakota, dakota-iso, zirconium-hawaii, bootc, and the odd third-party
#     source tree), quoted here as a source citation. These will never exist in
#     this tree. Prefer naming the owner in the prose too — a bare backticked
#     upstream path reads as a first-party one.
#   - Paths and tasks this repo deliberately cites as *absent*: deleted on
#     purpose, or proposed and never built, where the citation is the record of
#     that decision. Deleting the citation would destroy the record, so the
#     entry goes here instead (added by the #860 rot audit).
#
# Anything else is rot — fix the reference instead of listing it here.
#
# An entry ending in `/` covers everything beneath it. An entry prefixed
# `task:` is a mise task name, not a path.

# Planned, not yet written
docs/design/secure-boot-tpm-analysis.md   # output of docs/plans/2026-07-12-secure-boot.md Task 2 (#312)
docs/verifying-signatures.md              # planned by docs/design/cosign-keyless-signing.md § 5
docs/design/iso-distribution.md           # output of docs/plans/2026-09-16-r2-iso-hosting.md Task 5 (#867)
docs/plans/done/2026-09-16-r2-iso-hosting.md  # self-archive target of docs/plans/2026-09-16-r2-iso-hosting.md Task 6, once R2 hosting ships (#867)

